    {
      "id": "s5",
      "concept": "second-law-of-thermodynamics",
      "narration": "The second law of thermodynamics states that entropy in an isolated system never decreases. It always increases or stays the same, reflecting the natural direction of time and energy dispersal. This law explains why heat flows from hot to cold, not the reverse.",
